condition better over time.

00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:13.700
So that's why doing
a prospective study

00:05:14.620 --> 00:05:16.920
would really improve these results but

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:19.490
they do still say that they believe that

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:23.920
for a patient that's
hospitalized for COVID,

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:26.440
and that has type 2 diabetes,
one thing that definitely

00:05:26.440 --> 00:05:29.990
could help would be to
manage their blood glucose

00:05:29.990 --> 00:05:30.823
in real time.

00:05:33.750 --> 00:05:36.223
- Oh, yeah, that's
probably pretty critical.

00:05:37.877 --> 00:05:39.903
So what about,

00:05:41.560 --> 00:05:44.700
diabetes has its own set
of comorbidities, right?

00:05:44.700 --> 00:05:48.020
You have lots of heart
disease issues related to

00:05:48.020 --> 00:05:51.843
the diabetic kind of milieu as they say.

00:05:53.650 --> 00:05:54.583
- [Viktor] Absolutely.

00:05:56.020 --> 00:05:59.623
- Were there any indication in terms of,

00:06:00.510 --> 00:06:03.280
the presence of cardiovascular disease

00:06:03.280 --> 00:06:07.300
or specific demographics,
like age or other types

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:10.430
of medications that they're
taking that maybe not related

00:06:10.430 --> 00:06:13.973
to diabetes, was there any
indication that patients were,

00:06:15.030 --> 00:06:18.970
I guess, was there any
summary of patient history

00:06:18.970 --> 00:06:22.370
in how those factors could
have also impacted outcomes?

00:06:22.370 --> 00:06:24.070
Or did the paper not go into that?

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:27.910
- So the paper did go into it.

00:06:27.910 --> 00:06:32.470
But for the really big results,
were the graph that showed

00:06:32.470 --> 00:06:34.640
the survival rates, they actually adjusted

00:06:34.640 --> 00:06:37.393
for other comorbidities
like heart disease,

00:06:38.450 --> 00:06:42.260
liver disease, so they tried
to only focus on diabetes.

00:06:42.260 --> 00:06:45.260
Although they did mention
that those kinds of conditions

00:06:45.260 --> 00:06:48.890
and comorbidities typically
come with type 2 diabetes

00:06:48.890 --> 00:06:52.400
and are present in people
who do have type 2 diabetes

00:06:52.400 --> 00:06:55.220
and they do say that these factors,

00:06:55.220 --> 00:06:57.560
that can impact morbidity,

00:06:57.560 --> 00:07:01.040
but that wasn't the focus
up there, obviously.

00:07:02.640 --> 00:07:03.473
- Cool, thanks.

00:07:03.473 --> 00:07:04.840
And that was from Peggy from Facebook.

00:07:04.840 --> 00:07:06.740
So thank you for asking that question.

00:07:07.630 --> 00:07:09.167
