from this paper to currently

00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:45.333
treat individuals who have
COVID-19 and type 2 diabetes.

00:07:46.670 --> 00:07:48.170
Although I'm not exactly sure.

00:07:50.290 --> 00:07:52.210
- So we have a question from Susan,

00:07:52.210 --> 00:07:54.320
who's one of our RockEDU moms.

00:07:54.320 --> 00:07:55.153
So, hi, Susan.

00:07:55.153 --> 00:07:58.042
Thank you for your question.

00:07:58.042 --> 00:08:02.793
'Why was the group limited
to ages between 18 and 75?'

00:08:05.050 --> 00:08:09.810
- So the reason they limited the cohorts

00:08:09.810 --> 00:08:13.110
in the delineation of
age basically is because,

00:08:13.110 --> 00:08:17.760
so first for individuals
who are above the age of 75,

00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:21.060
these individuals typically
have a bunch of other

00:08:21.060 --> 00:08:22.260
kind of conditions,

00:08:22.260 --> 00:08:27.260
which could actually be
confounding factors for the study.

00:08:27.450 --> 00:08:29.450
So those individuals were eliminated.

00:08:29.450 --> 00:08:33.080
And then people who
were under the age of 18

00:08:33.080 --> 00:08:36.670
could also have a lot of these factors.

00:08:36.670 --> 00:08:41.670
But also, I would imagine that,
there must be some law for

00:08:41.870 --> 00:08:44.314
individuals who are under
18 to not be consenting.

00:08:44.314 --> 00:08:45.436
- Consenting.

00:08:45.436 --> 00:08:47.150
- Consenting.
- Consenting.

00:08:47.150 --> 00:08:50.430
- Yeah, I wonder we have in the
United States the age of 18,

00:08:50.430 --> 00:08:55.363
as like the sort of that barrier
between childhood and adult

00:08:55.363 --> 00:09:00.013
is that a universal age across the world?

00:09:00.013 --> 00:09:00.846
That's something I
