some places I think it's 16.

00:09:03.690 --> 00:09:04.744
- [Viktor] Yeah.

00:09:04.744 --> 00:09:05.577
- In some countries.

00:09:05.577 --> 00:09:06.840
- Okay, interesting.

00:09:06.840 --> 00:09:07.673
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:09:07.673 --> 00:09:10.000
- So I wonder what it is in China.

00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:13.460
I'm ignorant when it comes to
that stuff, so I apologize.

00:09:13.460 --> 00:09:14.880
- Yeah, I actually, I'm not sure either,

00:09:14.880 --> 00:09:18.052
but I think the main reason
is because these ages could

00:09:18.052 --> 00:09:21.870
represent confounding factors
in the analysis of the data.

00:09:21.870 --> 00:09:23.920
- Yeah, yeah.

00:09:23.920 --> 00:09:25.140
- Good point.

00:09:25.140 --> 00:09:29.730
Another question, do you
think or is there a difference

00:09:29.730 --> 00:09:32.070
in the lungs of people
with type 2 diabetes?

00:09:32.070 --> 00:09:34.530
I think this is pointing
at the fact that COVID-19

00:09:34.530 --> 00:09:38.956
seem to inflict on lung
cells more than other cells

00:09:38.956 --> 00:09:40.050
in the body.

00:09:40.050 --> 00:09:43.077
- Yeah, so they actually did
talk a little bit about this,

00:09:43.077 --> 00:09:47.010
in the paper, saying that individuals

00:09:47.010 --> 00:09:49.920
who have really advanced type 2 diabetes,

00:09:49.920 --> 00:09:51.970
particularly the individuals who have

00:09:51.970 --> 00:09:56.075
the poorly controlled blood
glucose often have damage in

00:09:56.075 --> 00:10:00.430
their vascular systems as
well as in their related

00:10:01.870 --> 00:10:05.990
lung systems, so the paper
does mention that they think

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:08.920
that's actually where the comorbidity

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:12.090
for the respiratory illness
comes from is the degradation

00:10:12.090 --> 00:10:14.670
of vascular as well as respiratory systems

00:10:14.670 --> 00:10:16.173
as a result of diabetes.

00:10:19.870 --> 00:10:21.530
- So we have a question from Chloe,

00:10:21.530 --> 00:10:26.530
who was d4p fellow,
one, three sessions ago,

00:10:27.470 --> 00:10:28.540
if you're including this one.

00:10:28.540 --> 00:10:31.490
So welcome back, Chloe,
thank you for joining.

00:10:31.490 --> 00:10:35.107
The question is, did all type
2 diabetic patients receive

00:10:35.107 --> 00:10:39.417
the same standard care
for COVID-19, and if not

00:10:39.417 --> 00:10:42.727
did the survival analysis
showing differences between

00:10:42.727 --> 00:10:45.617
the well and control
patients account for that?

00:10:47.826 --> 00:10:52.040
- So the treatment was very uniform

00:10:52.040 --> 00:10:54.970
for just COVID-19 patients in general,

00:10:54.970 --> 00:10:59.930
but the differences came
when the patients had

00:10:59.930 --> 00:11:00.820
severe outcomes.

00:11:00.820 --> 00:11:04.820
So if, for example, they
had the like ARDS syndrome,

00:11:04.820 --> 00:11:07.720
which was the acute
respiratory distress syndrome,

00:11:07.720 --> 00:11:10.620
then they of course had to
have different treatments

00:11:10.620 --> 00:11:14.813
than did other patients.

00:11:16.620 --> 00:11:19.820
What they did was they didn't compare

00:11:19.820 --> 00:11:23.000
directly patients who
basically didn't have

00:11:23.000 --> 00:11:24.720
the same treatments.

00:11:24.720 --> 00:11:27.210
So they delineated it in that way to

00:11:27.210 --> 00:11:29.263
remove that as like a confounding factor.

00:11:30.400 --> 00:11:33.320
Of course, you can't remove all factors

00:11:33.320 --> 00:11:34.460
that confound the analysis,

00:11:34.460 --> 00:11:36.810
but I think they try
their best in that regard.

00:11:39.950 --> 00:11:44.593
- Great, and question from Mackenzie.

00:11:45.607 --> 00:11:50.607
So can you talk more about
why poor BG, blood glucose,

00:11:53.457 --> 00:11:58.457
control exasperates COVID-19
from physiology perspective?

00:12:01.950 --> 00:12:04.890
- Yeah, so they're really
a plethora of reasons.

00:12:04.890 --> 00:12:09.033
So when you have a really
poorly controlled blood glucose,

00:12:10.070 --> 00:12:13.530
it means that you're either
not getting enough insulin

00:12:13.530 --> 00:12:18.100
or your condition is
maybe really advanced.

00:12:18.100 --> 00:12:21.170
So in this case, a few
things can be happening.

00:12:21.170 --> 00:12:25.480
So as a result of all the
glucose in your blood again,

00:12:25.480 --> 00:12:26.880
it can cause a lot of damage

00:12:28.240 --> 00:12:32.260
to your vasculature, it can
cause damage to your nerves,

00:12:32.260 --> 00:12:35.590
it can cause a bunch of
damage to multiple organs.

00:12:35.590 --> 00:12:36.830
And then, of course,

00:12:36.830 --> 00:12:38.810
since the cells ain't
getting enough glucose

00:12:38.810 --> 00:12:41.870
there can be, a huge, chemical cascade,

00:12:41.870 --> 00:12:46.080
where a bunch of issues
can occur just because

00:12:46.080 --> 00:12:48.850
a lot of processes that
typically will be occurring

00:12:48.850 --> 00:12:50.190
or won't be occurring.

00:12:50.190 --> 00:12:51.853
So then as a result of all this,

00:12:53.080 --> 00:12:57.300
a bunch of different diseases
can manifest actually

00:12:57.300 --> 00:12:59.710
from type 2 diabetes like I mentioned,

00:12:59.710 --> 00:13:02.700
like liver disease, kidney
disease and stuff like that.

00:13:02.700 --> 00:13:04.830
And then what happens then is

00:13:06.960 --> 00:13:08.660
a bunch of things happen, but then

00:13:09.590 --> 00:13:12.730
your immune system can also
really become compromised.

00:13:12.730 --> 00:13:15.880
And we know that from that

00:13:17.250 --> 00:13:20.173
you can have really severe
outcomes from COVID-19.

00:13:21.120 --> 00:13:23.570
Yeah, and in general, the answer is,

00:13:23.570 --> 00:13:24.510
there's a lot of reasons.

00:13:24.510 --> 00:13:26.780
But I think the main
reason is just because

00:13:28.050 --> 00:13:30.450
your systems basically just start failing

00:13:30.450 --> 00:13:32.720
and then your immune
system is compromised,

00:13:32.720 --> 00:13:35.280
and then you're just more susceptible to

00:13:36.690 --> 00:13:38.750
severe outcomes through COVID.

00:13:40.740 --> 00:13:42.321
- And I think
- I think,

00:13:42.321 --> 00:13:43.600
go ahead.

00:13:43.600 --> 00:13:46.280
- Along those lines,
do you think medication

00:13:46.280 --> 00:13:48.793
might have anything to do with that?

00:13:50.150 --> 00:13:52.840
Like so people with type 2
diabetes are taking medications

00:13:52.840 --> 00:13:55.743
that might alter certain
other aspects in the body?

00:13:56.600 --> 00:14:00.233
- Yeah, I definitely think
that is a factor for sure.

00:14:01.980 --> 00:14:05.680
However, I'm not really exactly sure about

00:14:07.140 --> 00:14:10.980
the specifics, although
the study did show that,

00:14:10.980 --> 00:14:14.913
even though the poorly
controlled blood glucose group,

00:14:16.060 --> 00:14:17.560
were given more medications,

00:14:18.540 --> 00:14:23.000
they did survive less than the well-controlled group

00:14:26.000 --> 00:14:27.580
- I think we're gonna end

00:14:27.590 --> 00:14:29.890
with one last question from Aditi.

00:14:29.890 --> 00:14:32.103
Thank you for joining us, once again.

00:14:33.000 --> 00:14:34.240
So happy to have you back with us.

00:14:34.240 --> 00:14:38.930
I think you might have the
frequent flyer card for d4p

00:14:38.930 --> 00:14:40.280
at this point in time.

00:14:40.280 --> 00:14:43.290
I think one day maybe we'll
get you a free coffee out it

00:14:44.250 --> 00:14:45.312
for ice cream.

00:14:45.312 --> 00:14:46.440
(chuckling)

